      "content": "You can steelman the affirmative by arguing that enhanced border security and stricter enforcement are mandatory preconditions for the nation's democratic and economic stability. First, a more fortified border directly reduces the volume and lethality of illegal drug trafficking and human trafficking, thereby protecting public safety and allowing law enforcement to operate more effectively. Second, robust enforcement acts as a critical economic safeguard by preventing the depletion of the workforce necessary to build and maintain the very infrastructure that supports the border and the nation as a whole. These measures do not inherently oppose all immigration but instead create a transparent, rule-based system that wets the harmonic for lawful, vetted migration while filtering out uncontrolled, dangerous influxes. Ultimately, strong borders are the only viable path to ensuring that the American experiment remains secure and sovereign without compromising on its core values.",
